<title>NEW ZEALAND: Power NZ arranges NZ$100 mln loan facility.</title>
<headline>Power NZ arranges NZ$100 mln loan facility.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Power New Zealand on Wednesday said it had arranged a NZ$100 million standby loan facility through three major trading banks: Bank of New Zealand, National Bank and ANZ.</p>
<p>The chairman of Power NZ, Don Stanley, said the company would draw down the facility as required to fund investment decisions.</p>
<p>The facility was being managed by the BNZ.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
